glibc on powerpc64le with clang instead of GCC.
Makefiles: no -m[no-]gnu-attribute, -msoft-float for -ffixed-<n> (`with-clang` from configparms).
ieee754.h, math_ldbl.h: no __ibm128 <-> long double conversion, no fr-pinned asm operands.
math.h __MATH_TG1, math-underflow.h, iscanonical.h: clang type-checks every _Generic arm and
cannot convert _Float128 <-> IBM long double, so select the function first, call once.
floatn.h: f128 builtin names, not GCC 6's *q. string-fza.h: cmpb is __builtin_ppc_cmpb.
sqrtf128: no "v" constraint, use __builtin_sqrtf128. soft-fp.h only below POWER9.
s_fsqrt.c: clang predefines __fsqrt (XL intrinsic).

